-- title:
--   Correctness of the coherent middle flag operation
-- statement:
--   For a G₂ verifier V and a prepared workspace assignment s(j,c), let K_tag embed the workspace with its six range tags computed. The literal middle program implements the logical middle permutation on this tagged fiber:
--
--   $$
--   U_{\mathrm{mid}}K_{\mathrm{tag}}
--      =K_{\mathrm{tag}}P_{\mathrm{mid}}.
--   $$
--
--   Here P_mid toggles the flag when range tag 3 is active, the clock is below its final value, and the verifier output bit is one. All other logical registers and the tagged workspace are preserved. This is the acceptance-controlled flag operation between the forward and inverse verifier calls.
